From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:05:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Show the ME state in setup and SMBIOS

The setup can turn the Intel ME off (me_state, which the CSE driver
applies at PCI enumeration), but nothing showed what the ME then did:
only the boot log has its status registers (dump_me_status() at
BS_OS_RESUME_CHECK exit), and with the ME disabled the OS has no HECI
device to ask.

me_status.c reads HFSTS1-6 once when the tables are written, SMBIOS
first and then the setup menu, at BS_WRITE_TABLES: HECI1 is still
visible then, as nothing hides it before BS_PAYLOAD_LOAD here. The
visibility is checked quietly (is_cse_enabled() warns when the device
is hidden), no HECI message is sent, and the options are read as the
CSE driver reads them, with UINT_MAX when there are none.

- General > About this ThinkCentre gets a read-only "Management Engine"
  line: "Disabled (soft temporary disable)", "Enabled", "Enabled, not
  ready (state N)", "Security override (jumper)" or "(HECI message)",
  "Debug", "Mode N", or "Not available" when HECI1 cannot be read. Its
  help has the registers, the working state, operation state and mode
  and the error code, that HECI is hidden from the OS when the ME is
  disabled, and the state the setup asks for when the ME is not in it,
  with what to do after three resets did not change it.
- SMBIOS type 11 OEM strings, through the root device's
  get_smbios_strings: "ME: <the same text>" and "ME HFSTS: " with the
  six registers, 64 characters at most each, for dmidecode and
  tools/update.py status.

TEST=Built me_status.c with the summary and SMBIOS code on the host
against stubbed registers: the live M920x values (80032044 368A0106
00000030 00004000 00000000 C0000004) give "Disabled (soft temporary
disable)", working state 4, operation state 1, mode 3, error code 2,
and a 63-character HFSTS string; the other modes, a hidden HECI1 and a
requested state the ME is not in give the expected text. Host syntax
check of the changed files; tools/cfr-dump.sh: the menu is valid with
info_me in About. For the hardware test: the line and its help in the
setup, the same registers in cbmem -1, the two strings in dmidecode -t
11, one more SMBIOS structure and nothing else changed, 00:16.0 still
absent from lspci.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
